{
  "_comment": [
    "Expected fixed obligations for finances_recurring. Data, not code: correct an",
    "amount or an end date here and redeploy the config, no Python change needed.",
    "Seeded 2026-07-30 from the finances repo's PLAN.md 'Known fixed expenses' table.",
    "",
    "Fields per item:",
    "  name             human label used in the checklist output",
    "  amount           expected amount in DOLLARS (positive = money out)",
    "  tolerance        +/- dollars still counted as MATCHED; use a wide band for",
    "                   variable bills (utilities) so normal seasonality isn't",
    "                   reported as CHANGED every month",
    "  expected_day     day of month the charge normally posts (1-31), or null if",
    "                   it floats; used only to order the checklist and to report",
    "                   how far off a match landed",
    "  match_any        payee substrings, case-insensitive. A transaction matches",
    "                   if ANY substring appears in its payee OR notes. Actual's",
    "                   payee strings are what SimpleFin delivers, so several of",
    "                   these are deliberately ugly (see 'Elec Ext Loan').",
    "  accounts         optional account-name substrings to restrict the search;",
    "                   omit to search every on-budget account",
    "  ends             final month the obligation is expected, 'YYYY-MM', or null",
    "                   for open-ended. Past its end month the item is reported as",
    "                   ENDED rather than MISSING, so a finished loan stops",
    "                   generating false alarms forever."
  ],

